Added in f237369:
- mixed case: `test_logprob_token_ids_with_topk_logprobs` (top-k `logprobs=1` with up to 4 `logprob_token_ids`, requests with and without ids);
- adaptive verification: `test_logprob_token_ids_with_adaptive_verification` (device `cu_num_logits`, host-side upper bound) checked against the fixed-boundary layout;
- `test_get_logprobs_dims_with_only_token_ids`;
- sharded gather: `test_gather_sampler_output_logprobs_and_nans` is now parametrized over top-k only, token-ids only and token ids wider than top-k.

The last one covers `gather_sampler_output` with those dims, not the `model_runner` call site, which I couldn't exercise without a TP>1 run.
I also re-ran the end-to-end check on a single GPU with MTP3 (chat streaming next to `/v1/systemone`): 0 errors, answers match a cold/cached call to within noise, accuracy unchanged.

